Removed the hardcoded `-webkit-mask` pseudo-element overlay (`.VPNavBarTitle .title::after`) and updated [docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css](docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css#L220-L229) with clean class-based logo styling:

```css
.VPNavBarTitle .title {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
}

.VPNavBarTitle .logo {
  height: 24px;
  width: auto;
  transition: opacity 0.25s;
}
```

### Why this resolves localized logos:
- **Exact Native Geometry**: Non-Latin script wordmarks (Arabic, Greek, Hebrew, Chinese, Armenian, Russian, Thai, etc.) ship purpose-drawn SVG assets with script-specific viewBoxes, dimensions, and dot placements. Removing the single-viewBox mask overlay lets each localized logo image (`logo-light-el.svg`, `logo-light-ar.svg`, `logo-light-he.svg`, etc.) render its native dot and wordmark accurately in both LTR and RTL.
- **Verification**: Regenerated [docs/.vitepress/theme/generated/site-themes.css](docs/.vitepress/theme/generated/site-themes.css), verified rendering in LTR and RTL modes, and passed all linter checks (`vp check --fix`) and docs unit tests (`vp test docs`).

